  bootwright / render
      Render external-tool artifacts. Without --input-dir or --output-dir, print this help.
      Context-free rendering requires both paths and conflicts with --context and --sensitive.
      Context-backed rendering requires --output-dir and --sensitive. This command is
      recognized but not implemented.

  Usage
    bootwright render [flags]

  Commands
  COMMAND     PURPOSE
  effective   Show normalized effective desired state
  installer   Render container-cluster installer artifacts (unavailable)
  storage     Render storage artifacts (unavailable)

  Command flags
      --clusters    Select comma-separated cluster names (default: all)
      --input-dir   Read a context-free input file or directory
      --output-dir  Write artifacts to the selected directory
      --sensitive   Authorize sensitive artifact materialization

  Common flags
      --ascii       Use ASCII status markers
      --color       Select terminal colors (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --context     Select a context (default: current context)
      --detail      Select human detail (values: compact, full) · default compact
      -h, --help    Show help for this command
      -o, --output  Select output mode (values: text, json, yaml) · default text
      --progress    Select progress animation (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --width       Set presentation width (0: automatic) · default 0
